sequenceDiagram
    participant H as Agent Host
    participant C as MCP Client
    participant S as Secured MCP Server
    participant L as Language Model

    H->>C: 1. Start the MCP Client
    C->>S: 2. Start or connect to the MCP Server
    C->>S: 3. initialize
    S-->>C: 4. Return protocol version and capabilities
    C->>S: 5. notifications/initialized
    C->>S: 6. tools/list
    S-->>C: 7. Return available tool descriptions
    C-->>H: 8. Provide tool descriptions
    H-->>L: 9. Make approved tools available
    L-->>H: 10. Select a tool and produce a tool call
    H->>C: 11. Send the approved tool call
    C->>S: 12. tools/call with tool name and arguments
    S-->>C: 13. Return tool result or error
    C-->>H: 14. Return the tool response
    H-->>L: 15. Make the response available
    L-->>H: 16. Produce the user-facing answer

    opt Host session ends or connection is no longer needed
        H->>C: 17. Close the MCP Client
        C->>S: 18. Close the transport connection
        S->>S: 19. Stop server process if client-managed
    end
